+# Matches HTTP and HTTPS web URLs. The host can be a domain name (with a TLD
+# of at least 2 letters), `localhost` or an IPv4 address, optionally followed
+# by a port, and then a path, query string and/or fragment without whitespace.
+url = Regex(
+    r"https?://(?:(?:[a-zA-Z0-9](?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}[a-zA-Z0-9])?\.)+[a-zA-Z]{2,}|localhost|(?:[0-9]{1,3}\.){3}[0-9]{1,3})(?::[0-9]{1,5})?(?:[/?#][^\s]*)?"
+)
+
 
 # The following regex is FRC 5322 compliant and was found at:
